# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
.nomedia

# Godot-specific ignores
.import/
export.cfg
export_credentials.cfg
*.tmp

# Imported translations (automatically generated from CSV files)
*.translation

# Mono-specific ignores
.mono/
data_*/
mono_crash.*.json

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Note: *.uid files next to scripts are Godot 4.4+ script identity and MUST be
# committed. They are deliberately not ignored here.

# Python bytecode from local syntax checks of .github/scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Control-plane scratch is NOT listed here, and should never need to be.
#
# The agent workflows (`.github/workflows/`, `.github/actions/`) write ~69
# scratch files per run. Every one of them goes to $RUNNER_TEMP, so none is
# ever written into the working tree and none needs an ignore entry.
#
# This briefly WAS a 69-name ignore list, added by #98 as a backstop while the
# conversion was in flight. It is gone because a literal-name denylist fails
# silently: rename a scratch file without renaming its entry and nothing goes
# red -- "Commit Leftover Changes" simply sweeps runner telemetry into
# somebody's pull request, which is what happened to #84 (eleven files of
# agent telemetry in the implementation commit, which then broke that task's
# retry). A file outside the working tree cannot do either, and needs nobody
# to maintain a list.
#
# `.github/scripts/test-workflow-logic.sh` Part 5 keeps it that way: a
# workflow that writes scratch into the checkout fails CI.
